/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5+(-1)(5) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(-1) & 1+(-1)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f1ad10-af76-57c6-940f-54720a66b04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 8 & 12 & 14\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056138} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6b2671-bf35-5e2b-8ae2-6ed3f7c4f920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 12 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 24 & 28\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056139} {:answer/id #uuid "e2588b59-90ef-5467-875e-c92359e99c71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056140} {:answer/id #uuid "0df38360-a680-533c-85cb-cbf6cc1b956d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056141} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc99020-ce13-5c21-9960-e34814529660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056142}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7e5993af-0e10-5818-81f9-6717646c2956" :answer-field/key "selection" :ans